{"id":16731,"name":"Jackson County","slug":"jackson-county","state":"Illinois","code":"IL","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-lien/tax-lien-states/illinois-the-best-tax-lien-state-with-36percent-return-on-investment/jackson-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-13T12:29:24","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Tax Lien","typicalSaleDate":"January","redemptionPeriod":"30 months","interestRate":"0-9% per year","bidProcedure":"Bid Down","extra":[{"label":"Contact for Sale Info","value":"Treasurer’s Office, Phone: 618-687-7350"},{"label":"Auction Site","value":"Jackson County Health Department , 415 Health Department Rd, Murphysboro, Il 62966"},{"label":"County Website","value":"Jackson County Official Website"},{"label":"Delinquent Tax Properties","value":"Jackson County Delinquent Tax Properties"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"From-9%-to-0%:-Jackson-County's-Bid-Down-Tax-Lien-Strategy\">From 9% to 0%: Jackson County&#8217;s Bid-Down Tax Lien Strategy</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed aligncenter is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"HbLzQiajK6y2cBnj2hlqPM8hRnuU634NgiFaefkEKUwCIZBCO41mXVt7msAzl01bp7d9\"><iframe title=\"From 9% to 0%: Jackson County, Illinois&#039; Bid-Down Tax Lien Strategy\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/3cqV4TFWINE?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p>Ready to Invest in Community Growth? Join the Jackson County Tax Lien Sale and Reap the Benefits of Your Investment! Jackson County, Illinois, offers an annual Tax Lien Sale, giving investors an opportunity to earn returns by purchasing delinquent property taxes. This process not only benefits the investors but also supports the community by ensuring tax revenues are collected.<br></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-understanding-the-process\"><strong>Understanding the Process</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>In Jackson County, the annual tax lien sale allows investors to bid on delinquent property taxes, not the properties themselves. The bidding starts at an interest rate of 9% and can go down to 0%. If you win the bid, you pay the owed taxes for that year. When the property owner pays back these taxes, you&#8217;ll receive the amount you paid plus the interest rate you bid. If the owner doesn&#8217;t repay within 30 months, you can petition the court for a tax deed, potentially acquiring the property at a fraction of its market value.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Key-Details-and-Links\">Key Details and Links</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Steps-to-Participate\">Steps to Participate</h3>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"1\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Understand Local Laws</strong>: Research the legal framework around tax lien sales in Jackson County to ensure you are familiar with the rules and regulations.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Visit the Local Treasurer&#8217;s Website</strong>: Check the County Treasurer’s Office for information on tax lien sales and other related details.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Check the Auction Site</strong>: Visit the County Auction Site to view upcoming auctions and register to bid.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Read the Auction Details</strong>: Understanding the sale schedule, parcel details, and auction rules is crucial.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Contact the County Office</strong>: For any additional inquiries, contact the Treasurer&#8217;s Office at 618-687-7350.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse-768x512.webp 768w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse-20x13.webp 20w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse-32x21.webp 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse.png 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse-541x360.png 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse-296x197.png 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse-768x512.png 768w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse-20x13.png 20w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Jackson-County-Courthouse-32x21.png 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-16744 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Jackson County Courthouse\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Pro-Tips\">Pro Tips</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Start Small</strong>: Begin with a few properties to understand the process better.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Do Your Homework</strong>: Research the properties and the area thoroughly before bidding.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Stay Informed</strong>: Regularly check the county&#8217;s website and auction site for updates and new opportunities.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"FAQs\">FAQs</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: What is the interest rate range for Jackson County tax lien sales?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: The interest rate ranges from 0% to 9% per year, with investors bidding down the rate.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: How long is the redemption period?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: The redemption period in Jackson County is 30 months.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: What happens if the property owner does not redeem the taxes?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: If the property owner does not redeem the taxes within 30 months, the tax buyer can request a tax deed for the property.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Useful-Links\">Useful Links</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.jacksoncounty-il.gov/263/Treasurer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">County Trea